<title>USA: ComEd Ill. nuke to restart late Tuesday.</title>
<headline>ComEd Ill. nuke to restart late Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison's 1,105 megawatt (MW) Byron 1 nuclear unit, shut since Feb 14 for maintenance, is expected to restart late Tuesday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The unit was originally shut to repair a leaky feedwater pump gland.</p>
<p>The facility's adjacent unit, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>ComEd is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
